## Important lesson

A network timeout is an unknown outcome—not proof of failure.

Financial systems should first determine whether the original operation completed before retrying it. Idempotency, ledger verification, reconciliation and manual-review escalation prevent duplicated money movement and unresolved transactions from being ignored.

